{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>On the day.</b> The anklets, they are on the feet." "<b>The shin-pieces.</b> It has no cognate [in Hebrew], and some say they are on the legs." "<b>And the crescents.</b> Like the shape of the moon on a belt, from Aramaic derivation, and according to the opinion of the majority so too אֲגַן הַסַּהַר (Song of Songs 7:3)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "Resolved רבים as 'the majority'; could also mean 'the many' or 'most commentators.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:03.839639116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}